  "build_notes": [
    "CPython: extract Python-3.14.7.tar.xz. PCbuild/readme.txt, PCbuild/build.bat and PCbuild/get_externals.bat are the Windows build recipe. Its PCbuild preparation scripts cover OpenSSL/libffi/Tcl/Tk. The accompanying official SPDX identifies the exact bundled source-dependency snapshots. Extract those cpython-source-deps archives into the externals directories named by PCbuild/python.props and PCbuild/tcltk.props. Unmodified MSVC, Windows SDK, NASM and other general-purpose build tools are separate prerequisites.",
    "Pillow: the PyPI sdist is supplied unchanged. The release Git archive Pillow-12.3.0-build.tar.gz adds .github/dependencies.json, .github/workflows/wheels.yml, winbuild/build_prepare.py and all recipe patches missing from the sdist. Read winbuild/README.md and build.rst. The Windows wheel workflow calls build_prepare.py --no-imagequant --architecture=AMD64, then build_dep_all.cmd and cibuildwheel; consult the supplied workflow and pyproject.toml for options.",
    "Pillow dependencies: place supplied release archives in winbuild/depends under the filenames required by build_prepare.py (rename only the archive file where this manifest prefixes pillow-). Supplied release-archive bytes and notices remain unchanged. The libyuv Gitiles snapshot is the documented exception: its request-varying container metadata is deterministically repacked while file bytes, paths, executable modes, LICENSE and PATENTS remain unchanged. The WebP source comes from the official Google release bucket because the historical downloads.webmproject.org HTTPS hostname failed certificate validation.",
    "libavif: its supplied cmake/Modules/LocalAom.cmake, LocalDav1d.cmake, LocalLibyuv.cmake and LocalLibsharpyuv.cmake pin aom v3.14.1, dav1d 1.5.3, libyuv 644251f252a84bf8ce91ff0aca86a9b16b069ab8 and WebP v1.6.0. Extract libaom-3.14.1 from its official release archive as libavif ext/aom, and extract the other supplied sources to ext/dav1d, ext/libyuv and ext/libwebp, to use the documented local-source paths. The deterministic libyuv tar has no enclosing top directory; its file contents and executable modes match the pinned Git tree.",
